Z||000000||Dslice||11-27-2001||02:17 AM||||On the 2.5l the car's idle doesnt drop it just seems to keep going up even after it heats up. We're talking up to 3000rpms. Besides the TPS what else causes this?<BR>The throttle isnt stuck either. I checked that.<P>Thanks,<P>------------------<BR>Rick<P>86GT<BR>84COUP<BR>http://home.mn.rr.com/gmfierogt||||reg||9
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-27-2001||02:30 AM||||Easy, you've got a vacuum leak. Check for a broken line. The 2.5s have few vacuum lines, so you outta spot it rather easily.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eriamjh||11-27-2001||07:23 AM||||I've had to replace the Idle Air control valve on my '87.  It's somewhere on the throttle body.<P>Also, put in a new GM PVC valve.  I've been told that helps.||||reg||1
